@startuml STM-4
!include _style.iuml
title STM-4 (System level) — Lifecycle of a TopUp\ntop_ups.status · v1.0 · 01/11/2026

state c1 <<choice>>
[*] --> pending : / send payment request
note left of pending
  created when the Driver confirms an
  amount within the limits (BR-P22) and
  has no other open top-up
end note
pending --> credited : payment confirmed\n[valid, amount matches, not yet applied]\n/ credit full amount, settle shortfall,\nredeem points, request e-invoice
pending --> failed : payment failed\nor Driver cancels
pending --> c1 : after(15 min)\n/ query gateway
c1 --> credited : [paid]\n/ credit, as above
c1 --> expired : [else]
expired --> credited : late payment confirmed\n[not yet applied] / credit once
expired --> [*] : after(1 h)
credited --> refunded : Admin refunds it\n[balance ≥ amount]\n/ debit credit, restore points,\ncreate refund (STM-10)
failed --> [*]
refunded --> [*]
note bottom of expired
  A payment confirmed after the 1 h window is
  recorded as a late payment (no credit, no invoice)
  and listed for Admin refund (STM-10, late_payment).
  A repeated payment result never changes the state.
end note
@enduml
